Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 02:58:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(nodes): flag nodes whose SMAC is inactive (F-37)

A SMAC is inactive when it has no record, or when its newest record across
last_smac_vc/pw/pf_values is older than SMAC_INACTIVITY_HOURS (3 h by
default, invalid values fall back to 3). GET /nodes now returns
smac_inactive per node: true/false, or null when the node has no
transformer. Falcon and SMAC thresholds share one config reader.

Unit tests cover the mapping and the threshold; an e2e test runs the
query on the isolated test database (2 h, 4 h, no record, newest table
wins, mixed transformers, no device).
